<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two South Korean flour mills, Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd and Cheiljedang Corp, bought on Friday a total of 22,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp, traders said.  </p>
<p>Officials of the two comapnies confirmed the deals but declined to give further details.</p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang bought 11,000 tonnes at basis over December futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for December 10-January 10 from the Pacific Northwest to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		4,500   $182.62</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,000   $186.29</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 4,500   $190.98</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  1,500   $195.94</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,000   $0.51</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 4,000   $0.66</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  4,000   $0.99</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
